---
description: pstack per-role model choices (overrides skill defaults)
alwaysApply: true
---
# pstack model configuration. One line per role. Do not delete a role line.
# `inherit-parent` or `auto` as a value: the role runs on the parent chat model (omit Task `model`). Alias entries in a panel list still count toward its fan-out.
# budget: medium (high). Hardest tasks stay at xhigh. Pass the role slug exactly. Do not raise, lower, or retarget it when spawning.
# Families are Grok and Composer only. Fast mode is off on every slug. No Claude, Opus, DeepSeek, GPT, or other third-party models.
# These lines are the Task `model` for every role, including subagents spawned by how, interrogate, swarm, arena, blast-radius, reflect, and any other skill.
# A missing ~/.cursor/rules/pstack-models.mdc does not restore a skill default. Use this file.
# Mechanical edits use composer-2.5 with fast mode off. Default reasoning uses grok-4.7-high with fast mode off. Only the hardest tasks use grok-4.7-xhigh with fast mode off.
# arena cross-judge pool is composer-2.5 so a Grok parent still has a judge from the other allowed family.
# interrogate reviewers is exactly one model.
# Never pass a model id containing -fast or fast=true to any subagent; when a skill asks for a fast/cheap model, use composer-2.5 non-fast instead.
feature, refactoring: composer-2.5
bug-fix: composer-2.5
perf-issue: composer-2.5
hillclimb: composer-2.5
judgment and prose: grok-4.7-high
hardest tasks: grok-4.7-xhigh
how explorer: grok-4.7-high
how explainer: grok-4.7-high
why investigators: grok-4.7-high
why synthesizer: grok-4.7-high
reflect tooling: composer-2.5
reflect judgment, divergent, synthesizer: grok-4.7-high
arena runners: grok-4.7-high
arena cross-judge pool: composer-2.5
swarm workers: composer-2.5
architect runners: grok-4.7-high
interrogate reviewers: grok-4.7-high
